title: **BSV Swift Exchange — Direct Deposit Flow**

note: **Peer-to-Peer Direct Payment**: The user's wallet constructs a transaction paying directly to the server's derived key. The server receives, validates, and broadcasts the transaction itself — **no address scanning, no watch addresses, no waiting for network propagation.**

_: **1. Wallet Connection & Identity**

User Wallet -> Frontend: Connect wallet
Frontend -> User Wallet: getPublicKey({ identityKey: true })
User Wallet -> Frontend: Return identity public key

_: **2. KYC Certificate Issuance**

Frontend -> User Wallet: Sign KYC authorization\n(protocol: `[2, 'KYC Authorization']`)
User Wallet -> Frontend: Signed authorization message

Frontend => Exchange Server: `POST /trustflow/verify`\n{ signedAuthorization, name }

note: Server validates signature, checks timestamp freshness (< 5 min), then screens against sanctions database

Exchange Server -> Sanctions API: `POST /match/default`\n{ name }
Sanctions API --> Exchange Server: { sanctioned: false, score }

Exchange Server -> BSV Network: `wallet.createAction()`\nBroadcast revocation anchor tx\n(1-of-2 multisig + OP_RETURN)

Exchange Server => Frontend: KYC Certificate\n{ subject, certifier, fields, revocationOutpoint }

note: Certificate stored in localStorage — valid 24 hours, revocable on-chain

_: **3. Construct Direct Payment**

note: **This is the key innovation.** The wallet builds a transaction that pays *directly to the server* using BRC-29 derived keys. No address is ever displayed or scanned.

Frontend -> User Wallet: Derive recipient public key\nBRC-29: protocol `[2, '3241645161d8']`\nkeyID: `{randomPrefix} {randomSuffix}`\ncounterparty: server identity key

User Wallet -> User Wallet: Generate random derivation nonces\nDerive unique one-time public key\nBuild P2PKH locking script

Frontend -> User Wallet: `wallet.createAction()`\n{ outputs: [{ lockingScript, satoshis }] }

User Wallet -> User Wallet: Sign transaction\nPackage as **AtomicBEEF**\n(tx + SPV ancestry proofs)

User Wallet -> Frontend: PaymentToken\n{ transaction (AtomicBEEF), derivationPrefix,\nderivationSuffix, senderIdentityKey, amount }

_: **4. Send Payment Directly to Server**

Frontend => Exchange Server: `POST /deposit` (BRC-103 authenticated)\n{ PaymentToken + KYC Certificate }

note Exchange Server: **Server-Side Validation (all in one round-trip)**

group: Certificate Verification
Exchange Server -> Exchange Server: Verify subject matches authenticated sender
Exchange Server -> Exchange Server: Verify certifier is this server
Exchange Server -> Exchange Server: Check certificate expiration
Exchange Server -> WhatsOnChain API: Check revocation anchor UTXO spent?
WhatsOnChain API --> Exchange Server: { spent: false } — certificate valid
Exchange Server -> Sanctions API: Re-check sanctions with certificate name
Sanctions API --> Exchange Server: { sanctioned: false }
end

group: Transaction Validation & Internalization
Exchange Server -> Exchange Server: `Transaction.fromBEEF()`\nParse AtomicBEEF envelope
Exchange Server -> Exchange Server: Derive expected BRC-29 key\n(`forSelf: true`, same protocol & nonces)
Exchange Server -> Exchange Server: Validate P2PKH hash matches\nderived public key hash

note Exchange Server: **The server now holds the valid, signed transaction**

-: **5. Broadcast & Credit**

Exchange Server => BSV Network: `wallet.internalizeAction()`\nAccept tx into server wallet → **broadcast to miners**

note: The SDK's Services layer submits the transaction directly to miners (ARC/TAAL). **No intermediary nodes, no address monitoring, no callbacks needed.**

Exchange Server -> Exchange Server: `balanceStorage.addBalance()`\nAtomic MongoDB `$inc` operation
end

Exchange Server => Frontend: { success: true, txid, depositAmount, newBalance }

Frontend -> Frontend: Update UI with new balance

=: **Deposit Complete**

note: **Total round-trips: 1** (client → server → miner). The user's balance is credited the instant the server validates and broadcasts. No polling. No watching. No waiting for block confirmations to detect payment.
